=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r1
diagnosis_text:
The affected subsystem is FRR (Free Range Routing) on the WAN gateway router r1. The mechanism is straightforward: r1 holds the only default route in the topology (`default via 203.0.113.1 dev eth2`, toward ISP ispa), and its FRR configuration contains `default-information originate`, which is designed to inject a 0.0.0.0/0 into the campus OSPF area 0. However, the FRR service is not running on r1 — pgrep finds no ospfd or zebra processes, and systemctl reports frr as inactive. Without a running ospfd, r1 never establishes OSPF adjacencies with csw1 (eth0, 10.0.0.34/30) or csw2 (eth0, 10.0.0.38/30); both core switches show zero OSPF neighbors on their WAN-facing interfaces. Because no default route enters the OSPF domain, neither csw1, csw2, dswa1, dswa2, dswb1 nor dswb2 has a 0.0.0.0/0 FIB entry. When pc1 sends any internet-bound packet, dswa1 (its VRRP gateway at 10.1.0.2) cannot find a matching route and returns ICMP Network Unreachable — confirmed by traceroute showing `!N` at the first hop. All internal campus paths remain fully healthy because those routes propagate correctly via OSPF between the running routers. The root cause is that FRR is inactive on r1, preventing the default route from being redistributed into the campus OSPF domain. The fix is to start the FRR service on r1 (`systemctl start frr`), which will bring up ospfd, form adjacencies with csw1 and csw2, and originate the default route so all campus routers can forward internet-bound traffic.
=== END ===